														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2502524">
									

<p>This doesn't work for me, because the Foundation should have enough basic competence incorporate allowances for the &quot;reality shock&quot; into the training, and not send someone out into the field to hunt a <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">werewolf</span> transmorphic humanoid when they were still that green. Which makes the final line pure lol-foundation.</p>
<p>It started out well, and for the first half, I was expecting to like it. But it went too far in how badly the Foundation reacted to their own training/preparation failure, and in how nonexistent that training and preparation seems to have been.</p>
<p>Strong start, weak finish. No vote.</p>

							</div>

								
